But they are not. AC is critical throughout the game, and especially in
the early game. The balance is to lower your AC before you level up.

I do pet test then try every piece of not cursed armor I can find. It's
amazing how many times you find a +4 orcish helm attached to some goblin.

WHen your AC is -20 it takes both a hit at 20 or more points of damage
to do any effect. In the early part of the game that means that most
monsters are just whiffing at you. This gives players the ability to
focus on the other aspects of game management.

The way to ascend is to stay ahead of the curve that the game naturally
throws. Get AC before you need it. Get MR before you need it. Get
reflection before you need it. Get weight management under control before 
you need to. Get holy water before you need it. Get wishes before you
need them. That's the whole game. Any character that acquires attributes
before they need them ascend a lot more often than not.

So it does require patience. It requires testing. It requires thought.

